-- title:
--   Valuation divisible by p: a=(1+p)^r wᵖ in ℚₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and let $a \in \mathbb{Q}_p$ be nonzero and such that the $p$-adic valuation $v_p(a) \in \mathbb{Z}$ of $a$ (Mathlib's `Padic.valuation`, the integer exponent with $a = p^{v_p(a)} u$, $u$ a unit) is divisible by $p$ as an integer. Then there are a natural number $r$ and an element $w \in \mathbb{Q}_p$ with
--   $$a = (1+p)^r \, w^p .$$
--   Thus every nonzero $p$-adic number whose valuation lies in $p\mathbb{Z}$ becomes, modulo $p$-th powers of $\mathbb{Q}_p^\times$, a power of the single element $1+p$; the exponent $r$ is produced as a natural number, not merely an integer, and $w$ is not asserted to be nonzero (though it necessarily is, since $a \neq 0$). The hypothesis $p \neq 2$ is genuinely needed: the corresponding statement for $p = 2$ is false, since $\mathbb{Z}_2^\times/(\mathbb{Z}_2^\times)^2$ has order $4$ and is not generated by the class of $1+2$.
--
--   This is the standard description of $\mathbb{Q}_p^\times/(\mathbb{Q}_p^\times)^p$ for odd $p$, where the subgroup of classes with valuation divisible by $p$ is cyclic of order $p$ generated by $1+p$ (equivalently $1 + p\mathbb{Z}_p = (1+p)^{\mathbb{Z}_p}$ together with the fact that $\mu_{p-1}$ consists of $p$-th powers). It is used in [`GaloisRepAdic.exists_root_one_add_prime_inertia_sub_mem_of_quotientScalar_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.exists_root_one_add_prime_inertia_sub_mem_of_quotientScalar_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle) to normalise a local unit up to $p$-th powers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Padic_exists_eq_one_add_prime_pow_mul_pow_of_dvd_valuation.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem Padic.exists_eq_one_add_prime_pow_mul_pow_of_dvd_valuation (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hp2 : p ≠ 2)
    (a : ℚ_[p]) (ha : a ≠ 0) (hv : (p : ℤ) ∣ Padic.valuation a) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (w : ℚ_[p]), a = (1 + (p : ℚ_[p])) ^ r * w ^ p := by sorry
